            <ArticleTitle>Otologic complications caused by hearing aid mold impression material.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>411-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.anl.2011.05.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two extremely rare cases of otologic complications caused by hearing aid mold impression material. The symptoms of patients with retained impression material are characteristic of the length of time the impression material is retained. In case 1 had a chronic discharge and granulation tissue of the middle ear, while case 2 presented with acute pain and dizziness. The management for retained impression material may require surgical interventions, which can be safely accomplished by standard otologic techniques.</AbstractText>
